## Architecture — The Bridge Model

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         TENNIS SUITE BACKEND                  │
│    Next.js API + Supabase + WebSocket         │
└────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
             │ REST + WebSocket
    ┌────────┼────────┐
    ▼        ▼        ▼
 Browser  Android    iOS
  (Web)    Phone     Phone
           │ BT       │ BT
           ▼          ▼
       Wear OS     watchOS
       Watch App   Watch App
       (Kotlin)    (Swift)
```

### Connection Logic Per Platform

**Android / Wear OS:**
- Watch connects **directly** to Tennis Suite API over Wi-Fi (standalone mode)
- Falls back to Bluetooth relay via Wearable Data Layer API when off Wi-Fi
- No phone app required for basic usage

**Apple Watch / watchOS:**
- Native `URLSessionWebSocketTask` (since watchOS 6)  
- Foreground-only — Apple kills background WebSocket connections  
- APNs push notifications handle background score alerts  
- iPhone companion app relays auth token via `WCSession`

