## What Gets Built This Sprint

### Part A — Watch API Endpoints (Next.js)

Ultra-compact endpoints returning minimal payloads:

```
GET  /api/watch/match/[matchId]          → live score state (~150 bytes)
GET  /api/watch/tournament/[id]          → tournament status
POST /api/watch/score                    → referee awards a point
GET  /api/watch/notifications/[userId]   → pending alerts
```

**Payload format** (optimized for watch bandwidth):
```json
{ "m": "Team A v Team B", "s": "3-2, 40-15", "srv": 1, "t": 1720595234 }
```

### Part B — Watch UI Simulator (Next.js /watch routes)

A **browser-based circular watch viewport** (390×390px) for design iteration without a physical device.

```
/watch                     → home / role picker
/watch/score/[matchId]     → referee point-scoring pad  
/watch/live/[matchId]      → live score display
/watch/alert               → notification feed
/watch/status              → tournament at a glance
```

### Part C — Wear OS Native App Scaffold

Kotlin + Jetpack Compose for Wear OS in `/watch-app/`:
- JWT auth via shared token from the web session
- OkHttp WebSocket client → `/api/watch/live/[matchId]`
- Haptic feedback on every point scored
- Tap +/− to award points (referee mode)

### Part D — Push Notification Bridge (Quick Win)

Wire FCM/APNs through the existing `/api/notifications` system:
- Score events → push → phone → **automatically mirrored to any paired watch**
- Works on ALL watch brands immediately, no native app needed
- Zero additional user setup

